# Deployment manifests for `{{ server_name }}`

These manifests deploy the generated MCP server onto a Kubernetes cluster that
has the [ToolHive operator](https://docs.stacklok.com/toolhive/guides-k8s/deploy-operator)
installed.

## You must provide external access yourself

These manifests do **not** include an Ingress, Gateway, or LoadBalancer. The
ToolHive operator creates a ClusterIP service on port 8080 (named
`mcp-{{ server_name }}-proxy`). Exposing it externally is your cluster's
concern — nginx-ingress, AWS ALB, GKE Gateway, Istio, etc. — and the URL
shape you pick must then match the placeholders in these manifests
(`audience`, `resourceUrl`, `embeddedAuthServer.issuer`, `redirectUri`).

See [Run MCP servers in Kubernetes](https://docs.stacklok.com/toolhive/guides-k8s/run-mcp-k8s)
for the operator's view of external access.

## Files in this directory

| File | When emitted | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mcpserver.yaml` | always | The `MCPServer` CRD that tells the operator to run this server |
{% if has_auth %}
| `mcpexternalauthconfig.yaml` | when auth is configured | Upstream API authentication (bearer token, or embedded OAuth/OIDC) |
{% endif %}
{% if is_embedded_auth %}
| `mcpoidcconfig.yaml` | embedded OAuth / OIDC only | OIDC issuer metadata that `MCPServer.spec.oidcConfigRef` points at |
{% endif %}
{% if is_api_key %}
| `secret.yaml` | API-key auth only | Kubernetes `Secret` holding the upstream bearer token |
{% endif %}

## Placeholders to replace before applying

{% if is_embedded_auth %}
- `REPLACE_ME_DOMAIN` — the external domain where the MCP server is
  reachable. Appears in `mcpserver.yaml` (`audience`, `resourceUrl`),
  `mcpexternalauthconfig.yaml` (`embeddedAuthServer.issuer`,
  `redirectUri`), and `mcpoidcconfig.yaml` (`spec.inline.issuer`).
  **All occurrences must agree and the URL shape must match how you
  expose the server** — see comments in `mcpexternalauthconfig.yaml`
  and `mcpoidcconfig.yaml` for the details.
- `REPLACE_ME` (in `mcpexternalauthconfig.yaml`) — the upstream OAuth
  app's `clientId`.
{% endif %}
{% if is_api_key %}
- `REPLACE_ME` (in `secret.yaml`) — the upstream API bearer token.
{% endif %}

In all configurations, the container image in `mcpserver.yaml`
(`{{ server_name }}-mcp:latest`) needs to be pushed to a registry
your cluster can pull from.

## Recommended apply order

The operator reconciles asynchronously, so out-of-order apply works — you'll
just see transient `NotFound` conditions on MCPServer until the other
resources are created.

{% if is_api_key %}
1. `kubectl apply -f secret.yaml`
2. `kubectl apply -f mcpexternalauthconfig.yaml`
3. `kubectl apply -f mcpserver.yaml`
{% elif is_embedded_auth %}
1. `kubectl apply -f mcpoidcconfig.yaml`
2. `kubectl apply -f mcpexternalauthconfig.yaml`
3. `kubectl apply -f mcpserver.yaml`
{% else %}
1. `kubectl apply -f mcpserver.yaml`
{% endif %}

Then expose the `mcp-{{ server_name }}-proxy` service externally with whatever
mechanism your cluster uses.
